Z||000000||lowfunds||06-04-2000||01:06 PM||||I was wondering just how reliable the 4speed manual trans. is for a v8 conversion? Has anyone had any trans failures with the v8? I hate to spent the time and money in a v8 buildup if the trans won't hold. Or would the 3800 conv. be the better way to go with the 4 speed auto that comes with the car? Any info. would be greatly appreciated. THANKS!!!!!<p>[This message has been edited by lowfunds (edited 06-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||06-04-2000||02:03 PM||||In my opinion, the 4 speed is one tough tranny, some people complain about the shifting being a little notchy though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan86gt3.8||06-04-2000||04:13 PM||||I think a regular naturall aspirated 3800 would perform better with a 4 or 5-speed, but the supercharged version I don't think it would matter.  Plus the auto is built to handle the power of the supercharger||||reg||1
