Z||000004||lowfunds||06-04-2000||05:28 PM||||OOps&gt; did not mean to post twice.. Does anyone know realistically how much hp a stock fiero trans will handle. I know alot depends on how you are going to drive. But let's be realistic who is going to put a v8 in one of our cars to baby it??? I want a setup that will handle a weekend trip to the drags once and a while(legal drag strip of course <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)and not leave me stranded at the line. Should I just drop the v8 idea and go with a supercharged 3800 with the factory 4speed auto???? once again thanks for any help.<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000005||batboy||06-04-2000||07:34 PM||||Don't worry about whether the tranny will handle the hp, it's the torque and how much it gets abused that will determine if it will hold up. Don't do burnout! Not even at the dragstrip. Drive around the water box. Burning rubber when you launch means you've lost traction, it's not good for anything but showing off and showing off we eventually break things. I'm speaking from experience when I used to do crap like that 15-20 years ago. As much as I love my 350 V8 sitting back there in my Batmobile, the 3800 is probably a better choice in the long run. Fits better, weighs much less than the 350, is very reliable, and fairly plentiful (the SC version is harder to find). They probably cost pretty close to the same amount for either swap (not counting the engine). I don't abuse my car (well, not too much anyway) and I still race it and have a blast.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jay||06-06-2000||04:42 PM||||What kind of V8 are we talking about here?  A 3800 is easier and less expensive to do, less down time, in my opinion.  I'd go with the supercharged version and use the stock auto tranny or if memory serves me correctly a Cavalier 5spd manual will bolt right up.  I know lots of guys that have both autos and 5 speeds with their 3800's||||reg||1
Z||000007||lowfunds||06-06-2000||07:43 PM||||The v8 I would run is a ZZ4 crate engine 355hp 400lb torque. the 3800 would be a 3800 supercharged intercooled engine running about 290-300 hp 300lb of tourque.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">))||||reg||1
